WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.102
-We're back with Colin Jost.

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:05.004
All jokes aside,
this is a really funny podcast

00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:07.273
you do with Wanda Sykes,
and it's getting great reviews.

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:10.977
-Um, yes, I was very --
Anything that gets good reviews

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:13.045
that I'm involved in,
I'm surprised.

00:00:13.045 --> 00:00:14.447
That's just my way
of thinking.

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:18.217
But people were
very excited about it.

00:00:18.217 --> 00:00:20.987
Our friend Claire Friedman
wrote it and she's fantastic.

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:23.255
I was very excited
to do it with Wanda.

00:00:23.255 --> 00:00:24.757
Wanda is in it.
Heidi Gardner is in it.

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:27.727
Cecily Strong, Neil Patrick
Harris, it's a great cast.

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:29.828
-You got Parnell.
-Parnell. That's right.

00:00:29.828 --> 00:00:33.766
I'm definitely the worst one
by a large margin.

00:00:33.766 --> 00:00:36.669
-That's not true.
But are you a little, um...

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:38.971
-I get suspicious.
-About the reviews?

00:00:38.971 --> 00:00:40.539
-The reviews.
Do you ever see reviews

00:00:40.539 --> 00:00:41.941
that they're so good
that you're like,

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:44.143
"This wasn't a human
that wrote this"?

00:00:44.143 --> 00:00:45.478
-Like, here's one. "Hilarious.

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:47.146
The character development
is so specific

00:00:47.146 --> 00:00:48.515
and the actors
are perfectly cast.

00:00:48.515 --> 00:00:50.183
I've laughed out loud
so many times

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:51.517
and can picture all of it."

00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:54.253
Five, five, five.

00:00:54.253 --> 00:00:56.856
-Five, five, five. Hilarious.
Also, I think also this is

00:00:56.856 --> 00:01:00.360
a little bit of a brag
about their own imagination.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.161
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.161 --> 00:01:04.564
You know? They're like,
"I can picture all of it.

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:06.265
You might not be able to."
-Yeah.

00:01:06.265 --> 00:01:08.568
You do feel like if there was
a second -- a fourth row

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:09.836
that said, like,
"my imagination,"

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:11.237
there'd be five stars there.

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:13.839
-It would be six.
"I imagine another star."

00:01:13.839 --> 00:01:16.109
-Yeah. "Funniest thing
I've heard in a while.

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:17.343
Claire Friedman is a genius.

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:19.078
Colin Jost and Wanda Sykes
are incredible together.

00:01:19.078 --> 00:01:20.513
Everything about
this is perfect.

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:22.215
It's like listening to
an amazing episode of '30 Rock.'

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:24.784
Cannot recommend enough"
is another one, all five.

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:26.852
-Genius. Claire Friedman,
a friend of mine.

00:01:26.852 --> 00:01:29.355
Would I say genius? Um...

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:31.257
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:33.459
"Colin Jost and Wanda Sykes
are incredible.

00:01:33.459 --> 00:01:35.094
Enjoying it is perfect.

00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:37.363
It's like listening
to an amazing episode," right.

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:39.598
And then I like that one person
found it helpful.

00:01:39.598 --> 00:01:41.467
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:44.136
-And I will admit, that was me.

00:01:44.136 --> 00:01:45.605
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:47.340
-I was like,
"This is very helpful for me."

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.408
-This is the -- This again,

00:01:49.408 --> 00:01:52.111
I would say with the words
still is positive.

00:01:52.111 --> 00:01:53.613
-Yes. "Hilarious.

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:56.815
I listened to this
in one day at work."

00:01:56.815 --> 00:01:59.986
Meanwhile, like, what's
the employer thinking right now?

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:03.356
That's like eight hours of work
that they spent listening to it

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:05.191
"and was literally
laughing out loud."

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:07.493
Overall, five stars
performance, five stars.

00:02:07.493 --> 00:02:10.497
Story, two stars.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.497 --> 00:02:13.132
So...
-Feels weird to be so positive

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:14.433
and then be like, "Story stunk."

00:02:14.433 --> 00:02:17.036
-Yeah, story. But anyway,
really, check out the story.

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:19.572
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.572 --> 00:02:21.674
I know you're like, "I bet
the story is going to be good."

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:23.108
It will be. Don't listen to...

00:02:23.108 --> 00:02:24.477
-I mean,
when you average it out,

00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:26.612
it's still like, you know, with
those other two fives,

00:02:26.612 --> 00:02:27.646
still comes out to like a four.

00:02:27.646 --> 00:02:30.283
-Probably like high threes.
-Yeah.

00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:32.585
-I'm no math guy.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.585 --> 00:02:34.854
-We didn't get into this
because we're math guys.

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:36.055
-Is it called math guy?

00:02:36.055 --> 00:02:37.557
-That was right before,
on that red carpet,

00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:40.092
someone asked you
what's 12 divided by 3?

00:02:40.092 --> 00:02:47.299
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:47.299 --> 00:02:48.968
Your mom had a birthday
or has one coming up?

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:51.337
-My mom's birthday
is on Sunday. I'm very excited.

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:54.306
-Very big fan of your mom.

00:02:54.306 --> 00:02:56.376
-Doctor Kerry Kelly.

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:57.810
She was in the fire department
for a long time.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.945
She's turning 21,
which is pretty exciting.

00:02:59.945 --> 00:03:02.181
-But how --
You did not know her age.

00:03:02.181 --> 00:03:03.449
-All growing up,

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:06.719
she would tell my brother
and I that she --

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:08.454
Every birthday, we would
be like, "How old are you?"

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:10.757
We don't ask now because
we don't want to know the truth.

00:03:10.757 --> 00:03:12.959
But when we were young,
we would ask like,

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:14.693
"How old are you turning?"
And she would always say,

00:03:14.693 --> 00:03:16.062
21 when we were kids.

00:03:16.062 --> 00:03:17.797
-Yeah.
-She was like, "I'm 21."

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:21.200
And you know
I'm a fairly gullible person.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.102
-Yeah.
-If you've ever seen me

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:26.973
on "Weekend Update" and perhaps
I've gotten tricked at times,

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:28.641
you may see me and say,

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:31.144
"That is -- I can't believe
how gullible this man is."

00:03:31.144 --> 00:03:33.379
-Yep.
-So as a kid I was also that.

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:35.114
And so when she would
tell me and my brother

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:36.715
she was turning 21 every year,

00:03:36.715 --> 00:03:42.721
I believed it for a very long
time, until I was like 12.

00:03:42.721 --> 00:03:45.424
And one of my friends asked
how old my mom was

00:03:45.424 --> 00:03:47.460
and I said, "She's turning 21."

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:50.296
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:52.699
And they were like,
"Oh, no, what happened?"

00:03:52.699 --> 00:03:55.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.534 --> 00:03:57.703
"Is she okay?
Is everything okay?"

00:03:57.703 --> 00:04:00.673
And I was like, "Yeah, it's
fine. She's 21, I'm 12."

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:02.141
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:04.276
And then they told their parents

00:04:04.276 --> 00:04:06.779
and then my mom had to be like,
"I'm 45, you idiot."

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:08.414
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:10.783
-You brought a photo of your son
Cosmo last time you were here.

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:12.151
-Yeah, he just turned --

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:13.953
He's two in a little bit,
a couple months.

00:04:13.953 --> 00:04:16.588
-Gotcha.
-And he's a cute kid.

00:04:16.588 --> 00:04:18.291
He's like -- He's doing
a lot of stuff.

00:04:18.291 --> 00:04:20.059
He's like, very active.

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:21.860
-Do you mind if we show a pic?
-No, no, no.

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:23.830
That's okay. Yeah.
Please go ahead.

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:26.965
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.965 --> 00:04:29.768
I feel like he has
his dad's sense of fashion.

00:04:29.768 --> 00:04:32.438
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:34.407
-Thanks.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:34.407 --> 00:04:37.576
Thanks for taking the time
to print that out to show that.

00:04:37.576 --> 00:04:39.378
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.378 --> 00:04:42.315
-I was like,
"I know what'll be funny."

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:45.050
-We are gonna --
When a guest insists on

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:46.819
making an art card
and it goes that bad,

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:47.987
we do make them pay for it.

00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:52.358
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:53.626
It's not much.

00:04:53.626 --> 00:04:55.594
-Yeah.
-It's not much, but we just...

00:04:55.594 --> 00:04:57.563
-I was like, "I got it."

00:04:57.563 --> 00:04:59.465
-I want to say --
I want to mention one member

00:04:59.465 --> 00:05:01.500
of your family
who recently passed.

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:04.003
And I say this with all
sincerity, your grandmother.

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:06.271
-Yes.
-Who I adored.

00:05:06.271 --> 00:05:08.074
And I remember the last time
I was lucky enough

00:05:08.074 --> 00:05:10.109
to get to talk to her
was at your wedding.

00:05:10.109 --> 00:05:12.211
And it was so exciting
that she was there.

00:05:12.211 --> 00:05:14.880
She passed away.
Tell everybody how old.

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:17.817
-My grandma just passed away.
She was 106 years old.

00:05:17.817 --> 00:05:19.451
[ Audience gasps ]
Yes.

00:05:19.451 --> 00:05:21.687
So it's not even --
No sympathy at that point.

00:05:21.687 --> 00:05:22.888
[ Laughter ]

00:05:22.888 --> 00:05:24.223
You tell people like,
"Oh, my grandma died,"

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:25.391
and they're like,
"Oh, my God, I'm so sorry.

00:05:25.391 --> 00:05:27.260
How old was she?"
And you're like, "106."

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:28.627
And they're like,
"Oh, so kind of late."

00:05:28.627 --> 00:05:32.364
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.364 --> 00:05:34.700
She was turning -- She was 106.

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:37.169
And she survived COVID.
Like, she got through COVID.

00:05:37.169 --> 00:05:39.572
And so I remember calling her
when COVID started and I

00:05:39.572 --> 00:05:42.175
was like, "Grandma, are you
okay? Is everything okay?

00:05:42.175 --> 00:05:45.678
And I swear to God, she was
like, "First the Spanish flu."

00:05:45.678 --> 00:05:50.817
[ Laughter ]

00:05:50.817 --> 00:05:52.919
"Now this."

00:05:52.919 --> 00:05:56.522
And I was like,
"How old are you?!"

00:05:56.522 --> 00:05:58.958
It's true.
It's literally the same years

00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:02.762
as if it had been like, "First
the Titanic, now the submarine."

00:06:02.762 --> 00:06:04.964
[ Laughter ]

00:06:04.964 --> 00:06:06.232
-May she rest in peace.

00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:08.100
She lived a long life.
We were lucky to have her.

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:09.902
-We were very lucky.
-I was very lucky to know her.

00:06:09.902 --> 00:06:11.637
Thanks for being here, buddy.
It is just the best.

00:06:11.637 --> 00:06:13.672
Have a great show.

00:06:13.672 --> 00:06:15.375
-Thanks for having me.
-That's Colin Jost, everybody.

00:06:15.375 --> 00:06:18.243
"Trust Fall" is on Audible now.
Audible.

00:06:18.243 --> 00:06:19.312
Check out "SNL" this week

00:06:19.312 --> 00:06:21.046
with host
Adam Driver and musical guest

00:06:21.046 --> 00:06:22.748
Olivia Rodrigo on NBC
and Peacock.

00:06:22.748 --> 00:06:24.384
We'll be right back with
Gael Garcia Bernal.

